z9x-0006: PIN brute-force throttle, per-attempt random PIN, local-peer admission hook

Ours (Z9xAirPlay), against FDH2/UxPlay master 3dbf7ce after z9x-0001..0005 (paths relative
to UxPlay/lib). Applied by jni/build_native.sh inside a copy of UxPlay/lib with
patch -p1 --fuzz=0.
- raop_handlers.h: 3 wrong codes lock PIN pairing for 30 s, doubling per lockout up to
  15 min (reset by a successful pairing); refused pair-pin-start / pair-setup-pin while
  locked. Random mode (pin < 10000): a code is issued by pair-pin-start and is valid for
  one wrong guess or 5 min; pair-setup-pin without a pending code is refused (UxPlay used
  "0000" in that case).
- raop.h: optional callbacks conn_admit (refuse a TCP peer by address) and pin_lockout.
- raop.c: throttle state in raop_t; conn_init asks conn_admit first.
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

